You can create an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) cluster with multiple worker nodes using Terraform. I recommend creating a cluster with a system node pool and a separate application node pool.

We will use the AzureRM Terraform provider and deploy:
- AKS Kubernetes cluster.
- System node pool for Kubernetes system components.
- User node pool for application workloads.
- Managed identity.
- Azure networking.
- Autoscaling configuration.
- Terraform outputs for cluster name and credentials.
